{"task_id": "Mbpp/87", "solution": "def validate_inputs(dict1, dict2, dict3) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if all three inputs are dictionary objects.\"\"\"\n    return isinstance(dict1, dict) and isinstance(dict2, dict) and isinstance(dict3, dict)\n\ndef merge_dictionaries_three(dict1, dict2, dict3) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"\n    Merges three dictionaries into a single dictionary, handling key conflicts by preferring the last dictionary's value.\n    Raises TypeError if any input is not a dictionary.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not validate_inputs(dict1, dict2, dict3):\n        raise TypeError(\"All inputs must be dictionary objects.\")\n    \n    merged_dict = {}\n    merged_dict.update(dict1)\n    merged_dict.update(dict2)\n    merged_dict.update(dict3)\n    \n    return merged_dict"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/90", "solution": "from collections.abc import Sequence\n\ndef len_log(words):\n    \"\"\"Compute length of longest word in words.\n\n    Args:\n        words: a list (or sequence) of str elements per SRS.\n\n    Returns:\n        int: number of characters in the longest string, or 0 if words is empty.\n\n    Raises:\n        TypeError: if words is not a sequence (list/sequence) or any element is not a str.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(words, Sequence) or isinstance(words, (str, bytes)):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 'words' must be a sequence (e.g., list, tuple) of strings, not a string or bytes object.\")\n\n    if not all(isinstance(word, str) for word in words):\n        raise TypeError(\"All elements in 'words' must be strings.\")\n\n    if not words:\n        return 0\n    else:\n        return max(len(word) for word in words)"}
